    "The government can redistribute income by taxing higher-income earners at higher average rates (a progressive income tax), which reduces the gap between high and low after-tax incomes, and by using the revenue to fund transfer payments (such as pensions and unemployment benefits) and services (such as public health and education) that benefit lower-income households proportionally more. Together the tax and transfer system makes the distribution of income more equal.",
