    "An appreciation of the Australian dollar means it buys more foreign currency. For Australian exporters, their goods become more expensive in foreign currency terms, so overseas demand for Australian exports tends to fall, reducing export revenue. For Australian importers and consumers, foreign goods become cheaper in Australian dollars, so imports rise.",
