    "The business cycle has four phases. The expansion (upturn) phase is when economic activity, output and employment are rising, up to the peak — the highest point of the cycle, where growth is at its strongest before turning down. The contraction (downturn) is when economic activity, output and employment are falling, down to the trough — the lowest point of the cycle, where activity stops falling before a new expansion begins.",
