    "Bounded rationality is the idea that people want to make the best decision but are limited by incomplete information, limited time and limited mental processing ability, so they often make 'good enough' decisions rather than perfectly optimal ones. For example, a shopper may choose the first acceptable product they find rather than comparing every option available.",
